cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GridSentinel in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "GridSentinel: Machine-Learning Detection of False Data Injection in Smart-Grid Substations"
abstract: >-
  GridSentinel is a defensive, fully synthetic toolkit that detects false data
  injection (FDI) attacks against power-grid state estimation and IEC 61850 GOOSE
  messaging. It combines a physics-based chi-square baseline with a stacked
  machine-learning ensemble (random forest, gradient boosting, neural network and
  isolation forest) over multi-domain features, and demonstrably catches the
  stealthy residue-preserving attacks the classical detector is blind to.
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
license: Apache-2.0
